# Deterministic line endings for the whole repo (backlog #48).
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` — git auto-detects text files and checks them out with
# LF endings on EVERY platform, overriding machine-global core.autocrlf
# settings (the source of the endless "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings
# on this Windows machine). LF is the canonical style: the agent file tools
# pin new files to LF (src/tool/agent/file_write.rs / file_append.rs) and
# file_edit matches any style, so a uniform LF working tree removes the
# whole mixed-ending failure class.
#
# Binary files must never be touched by the eol/text machinery.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images / media.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.avi binary
*.mov binary

# Fonts.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Executables / libraries / debug symbols.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary

# SQLite databases under .coding/ (memory, codegraph) + WAL/SHM sidecars.
*.db -text
*.db-wal -text
*.db-shm -text

# The backlog is jsonl (one item per line, UUID ids): concurrent backlog_add
# calls from multiple worktrees must merge by concatenation, never conflict.
# The union driver keeps BOTH sides' lines on a conflict — the UUID ids make
# the union collision-free (a duplicate id line would only occur if the same
# item was edited on both sides, which the store tolerates on load).
.coding/backlog.jsonl merge=union
